  "details": "VRChat should add some form of \"multi-instancing\", or really just \"Spectator Mode\" as known in other games. Or even further: Just better performance overall in an instance by reducing the quality of some features.\n\nPart of the problem of VRChat are instances sizes and performance. We already struggle to hit good performance with 40 players, and 80 players can be a slog at times. \n\nIt would be cool if a world can dedicate \"zones\" to specific areas of the world. Think about World of Warcraft and how their instancing system works. Being able to see players on another side of the map (even if just impostors or something) to make a instance feel more alive and immersive. And possibly even allowing you to seamlessly swap to that instance if you move to that area.\n\nThis is obviously a vague feature request, but it's kind of on purpose. I feel like there are dozens of ways to solve this problem. The core feature is just enabling ways to make instances feel more full.",
